@deluxe097 It is not.

@0x7763680a A 2 of 2 multisig is arguable worse than single sig, because it has TWO single points of failure. Lose either key and it's catastrophic loss.

@delvin_baronof I've written several articles about key generation / management / backups; they're all linked from https://t.co/GQPyJJSgfh

Backup recommendations for Casa users mostly come down to the difficulty in securing backups and not wanting a threshold of cleartext backups laying around.

Yes, there is nuance here.

I would NOT advise someone to just jump into architecting their own distributed multisig setup from scratch with no oversight, as there are plenty of footguns.

You should either spend a ton of time researching the design decisions and threat models, or use a guided setup that has been designed by folks who have.

